.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Trying to resolve the Fermi-Pasta-Ulam-Tsingou recurrence puzzle, Norman Zabusky and Martin Kruskal simulated the continuum (KdV) limit of a nonlinear oscillator chain in 1965 and watched a single generic disturbance -- not an exact multi-soliton solution -- &quot;fission&quot; into a rank-ordered train of solitary waves that then collided and emerged unscathed. kdv_evolve integrates the Korteweg-de Vries equation">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/fields/solitons/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_kdv_soliton_fission_thumb.png
